			"notes": "# Create: Buzzy Beez 1.6.0\n\n## New\n- **Optional block removal**: When placing a schematic where blocks already exist, you now get a choice what todo with those (break, replace, keep)\n- **AE2 and Refined Storage cable buses** in schematics are now built correctly.\n- **See what's out of reach**: parts of a job no hive can reach get a pulsing red box, and the job tells you how far the nearest hive falls short and what RPM it needs.\n- **Smarter material ordering**.\n\n## Performance\n- Rewrote how bees get their work increasing performance\n- Bees now use spare server tick time for placing blocks (**adaptive block budget**). Large builds go much faster on smaller servers and back off automatically when the server gets laggy.\n- Ghost blocks are now uploaded to the GPU once instead of rebuilt every frame, and only the part of the ghost that changed is updated.\n- Bees off screen or beyond the render distance are no longer drawn, and the number of bees drawn can be capped.\n- Many smaller server-side fixes\n\n## Changes\n- A job no longer stalls completely when part of it is out of range. The bees build everything they can reach and pick up the rest as soon as a hive can reach it.\n- Fluids are always removed first and placed last, including when undoing and redoing.\n- The next build phase now starts as soon as the previous phase's blocks are placed or removed, without waiting for bees to finish delivering items.\n- Stuck reasons now only appear once a problem lasts a couple of seconds, so they no longer flash briefly when joining a world.\n- Missing-material messages now show item names in your own language.\n\n## Fixes\n- Bees no longer hover for minutes over water or lava they're removing.\n- Removing a built schematic now also removes the fluids it placed (for schematics built from 1.6.0 on).\n- Zapper placements no longer try to place a block before the old one is removed.\n- Fixed a missing-texture error with some icons.\n\n## Config\n- New config options added for performance"
		},
