			"notes": "# Create: Buzzy Beez 1.4.1\n\n## AE2 & Refined Storage support\n- **Logistics Ports and Cargo Ports can now use a whole AE2 or Refined Storage network** as their storage. Attach a port to an ME Interface, or to any block of a Refined Storage network, and your bees can pick up from and drop off into the entire network.\n- **Autocrafting for missing materials:** when a bee job is missing materials, a pickup port on an AE2 or Refined Storage network asks that network to craft them. The crafted items land in the network, and the bees pick them up from there.\n  - Can be turned off or tuned in the server config (`autocrafting` section).\n\n## QoL\n- **Port bulbs now glow while bees use them**, in each port's busy colour, on Logistics, Cargo and Dock Ports.\n- **Goggles on a Logistics Port** show what's currently being crafted.\n- **Finish chime:** when one of your jobs is done, you hear a chime and see \"<name> finished\".\n- **Look at a job's area** to see its progress, how many bees are working on it, and why it's stuck if it is.\n- **Other players' jobs are now visible:** you can see the area outline of nearby jobs started by other players, along with who started them. Only the player who started a job can cancel it.\n\n## Fixes\n- Belts now show up in schematic previews (shift-right-click preview, job preview, Schematic Deployer preview).\n- Block entity previews are now capped at 100 per schematic (configurable), so previews stay fast.\n- Fixed a CurseForge upload issue.\n\n## Other Changes\n- The Logistics Port recipe now makes 2 ports.\n- New Copy Planner texture."
		},
