			"notes": "## Create: Buzzy Bees 1.4.0\n\nThe biggest update so far: new planners, a much stronger Schematic Zapper, fluids, Create logistics integration, undo/redo and fully reworked ponders.\n\n### New\n- **Copy Planner**: select an area, then copy or cut it and paste it somewhere else with bees. The clipboard is placed like a schematic and stays for more pastes (#56, #8)\n- **Master-Planner**: one item that acts as every planner, now including the Copy Planner and Create's Schematic and Quill (#58, #10)\n- **Undo / redo for bee jobs**: press Z / Y while holding a planner or the zapper. Bees carry out the undo themselves (#55)\n- **Schematic Zapper**: a survival Worldshaper whose work is done by bees (#50). It now has its own shapes, including Ellipsoid, Dome, Capsule, Cone and Torus, a hollow mode for balloon envelopes and airship hulls, and configurable size limits (#60)\n- **Fluid support**: the new **Dock Port** connects bees to fluid tanks. Bees place fluids from schematics and pick them up when deconstructing (#11)\n- **Waggle Port**: orders whatever bee jobs are missing from Create's logistics network and has it delivered to an address. Items kept in stock by Factory Gauges get crafted automatically (#61)\n- **Mechanical Apiary**: turns bone meal and flowers into honey. Honey and sugar compact into honeycomb (#54)\n- **Clipboard checklist**: right-click a schematic ghost with a Clipboard to write the missing items onto it (#51)\n- **Sable (Create Aeronautics) compatibility**: bees work on and around ships (#22)\n\n### Changes\n- **Bee springs matter now**: when a bee's spring runs out it flies home, rewinds and continues where it stopped. Faster hive rotation makes springs last longer; Portable Beehive rewinds cost honey (#62)\n- **Planner toolbar**: the Deconstruction, Pickup and Copy Planners share a Create-style toolbar (hold Alt and scroll) (#57)\n- **Planner reset and sounds**: shift-right-click clears a schematic, clipboard or selection, with new sounds for setting corners, clearing and programming (#59)\n- **Custom GUI textures** for the Waggle Port, Schematic Zapper, Schematic Deployer and the job detail panel, which now shows missing materials as item slots (#63)\n- **Shorter tooltips** and goggle titles for the Logistics and Dock Ports; the Dock Port got a new look (#65)\n\n### Ponders\n- Every ponder rebuilt in Create's style: Mechanical Beehive, bees and their spring, Logistics, Cargo, Dock and Waggle Port, and the Schematic Deployer, in new ponder categories (#64)\n- The Cargo Port ponder now explains requester priority and what happens when a requester is full (#53)\n\n### Fixes\n- Crash at startup when a config value was read too early (#3)\n- Server crash every time a Bumble Bee finished a transport job (#47)\n- Crash with bees and Cargo Ports (#2)\n- Bumble Bees weren't counted by their hive and could exceed the bee limit (#48)\n- Bumble Bees turned into Mechanical Bees after Pickup Planner jobs with a Portable Beehive (#46)\n- Bees kept retrying forever when their network disappeared (#66)\n- Create's Print tool on planners left the planner out of sync (#67)\n- Bulk gluing didn't work (#21)\n- Group assignment didn't allow selecting existing groups or the root (#6)\n- The flight upgrade interfered with other mods that enable flight (#4)\n- The GeckoLib dependency is now listed (#5)"
		}
